1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,000
MOHASHUNNYO: A LONG WAY HOME. Design a mission, read the planet, bring the crew home.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:12,000
Begin in the 3D Earth lab. Prepare equipment, balance resources and integrate the vehicle.

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:17,000
Choose your commander. The lab, crew, spacecraft and consoles are actual game scenes.

4
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:23,000
The Flight Lab teaches engineering decisions. NASA data and game assumptions are identified separately.

5
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:31,000
Go for launch. A real in-engine ignition and ascent carries the mission toward Mars.

6
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:41,000
Fly terminal descent, or use assisted landing. This clip shows the actual assisted flight model.

7
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:49,000
Cancel speed and drift, then confirm touchdown. Landing quality affects mission resources and science.

8
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:57,000
Follow visible objectives and collect observations. The live first-mission route remains beginner-friendly.

9
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:00,000
Hold E to scan. Instruments cost electricity, so choices have resource consequences.

10
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:05,000
Optional thruster demonstration: Ctrl+Space spends a finite charge while Mars gravity stays unchanged.

11
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:13,000
Controlled hazard showcase: red rings warn of fictional impacts. Move clear or reach shelter.

12
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:21,000
Staged outpost showcase: deployable power, oxygen, shelter, industry and research extend exploration.

13
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:26,010
Bring the evidence home. Real game footage, edited for this showcase; no generated imagery or voice.
